commit a60a79019b2aaddc5463d8b8d2c8bc1fdb10ab13

C03: the look-at-it order without an object gets its own clarification, validated against role inversion (DIALOGUE1489)

DIALOGUE1487 measured that «Quiero que lo veas y de que se trata?» asked «¿Qué quieres que vea?» through the generic missing-referent clarifier, but «Miralo y decime de qué se trata.» got «¿De qué se trata exactamente?» (the person's request asked back) and «Mirá esto y decime qué es.» got «¿Qué es eso que miraste?» (the looking attributed to the person). The order now has its own unresolved-input kind, `deictic_look` (moved out of `_standalone_deictic_request`), with a situation that says telling what it is about is BAXY's part and naming what to look at is the person's, and a validation with one corrected retry: the question must ask what BAXY should look at (a look verb with «qué/cuál») and may not return «de qué se trata» / «qué es eso» nor say the person looked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


